<DocsPageSection>
    <DocsPageSectionHeader Title="Animation" AddedVersion="2.4" AddedDate="2026-09-18">
        Set <Code>Animated="false"</Code> for immediate changes, or use <Code>AnimationDuration</Code> to adjust the duration in milliseconds.
        A null duration preserves the provider's default; zero or a negative value disables animations.
        Toggle the alert or use its close button to see the entrance and exit effects. The alert stays in layout until its exit animation finishes. Animations also work without a close button, and the initial visibility is applied immediately. Reduced-motion preferences disable the effects.
        <Code>VisibleChanged</Code> reports the requested visibility without waiting for animation completion.
        The effects use CSS display transitions and starting styles. Unsupported effects fall back to immediate visibility changes.
    </DocsPageSectionHeader>
    <DocsPageSectionContent Code="AlertAnimationExample" Outlined>
        <AlertAnimationExample />
    </DocsPageSectionContent>
</DocsPageSection>

<DocsPageSectionTitle>
    Best Practices
</DocsPageSectionTitle>

<DocsPageSubsectionTitle IncludeInToc="false">
    Make Messages Actionable
</DocsPageSubsectionTitle>

<DocsPageParagraph>
    Write a concise message that explains what happened and, when applicable, what the user should do next. Match the color to the message severity, but include meaningful text or an appropriate icon so color is not the only indication of status.
</DocsPageParagraph>

<DocsPageSubsectionTitle IncludeInToc="false">
    Feedback Pattern
</DocsPageSubsectionTitle>

<DocsPageParagraph>
    Alerts are appropriate for information that belongs in the current page and may need to remain visible. Make an alert dismissible only when it can be safely ignored, and keep blocking errors visible until the problem is resolved. For brief feedback about a completed action, use a <Anchor To="docs/components/toast">Toast</Anchor> instead.
</DocsPageParagraph>

